-- The provisions of the Act that three amending Acts changed between the Revised Edition 2003 and the Revised Edition 2012, and the Order that changed O 2 in 2022, on two days.
-- None of them is on the chain that decides whether a person needs a licence for a receiver (s 2(1), s 20, s 47, the First Schedule); `sgba-versions.l4` holds that chain on two days.
--   Act 55 of 2004 (Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004): s 48 repealed and re-enacted, and a new s 48A (in operation 1 January 2005, by S 750/2004).
--   Act 21 of 2005 (Companies (Amendment) Act 2005), Schedule item (3): s 35(3) (in operation 30 January 2006, by S 878/2005).
--   Act 15 of 2010 (Criminal Procedure Code 2010), Sixth Schedule item 8: s 55 (in operation 2 January 2011, by S 776/2010).
--   S 212/2022: sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2 of the Exemption (No. 2) Order (O 2) deleted (in operation 25 March 2022, its publication day).
-- The text before each amendment is the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003); the text after is read from the amending Act, and from the existing single-text rules of the Act's modules, which state the 2024 consolidation.
-- Compared by script (2026-11-04), the 2012 Revised Edition's ss 48, 48A and 55 differ from the 2024 consolidation only in drafting style ("shall" and "must", "he" and "the person", "referred to" and "mentioned"), and the 2012 Revised Edition's s 48 and s 48A read word for word as the 2004 Act prints them.
-- Two days, as in `sgba-versions.l4`: the day of the conduct, and the day the law is read as at. A version is read if it was published on or before the reading day and takes effect on or before the day of the conduct; the latest published of those is read.
-- ASSUMED, NOT RULED: the published day of an amendment made by an Act is the day the notification that appoints its commencement day was first published, because until then a reader of the Act could not tell from the Act when it takes effect.
--   Act 55 of 2004: the Act was first published on 14 December 2004 and S 750/2004 on 17 December 2004; Act 21 of 2005: 6 June 2005 and S 878/2005 on 30 December 2005; Act 15 of 2010: 21 June 2010 and S 776/2010 on 20 December 2010.
--   To use the Act's own first publication day instead, change the three `... was first published on` constants below to those days.
-- For s 55 the first day is the day the proceedings are conducted. Section 429(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 keeps proceedings begun before the appointed day under the repealed Code, and this module does not encode that (fork F-BA-13).
-- Where a rule has no version (a conduct day or a reading day before 31 July 2003, or a reading day after `the day the sources were last checked`), the answer is NOTHING.

§ `Reading a list of text versions`

GIVEN x IS A `Provision text version`
      y IS A MAYBE `Provision text version`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Provision text version`
`the later published of two provision text versions` MEANS
    CONSIDER y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
    WHEN JUST z THEN IF x's `published on` AT LEAST z's `published on` THEN JUST x ELSE JUST z

GIVEN versions IS A LIST OF `Provision text version`
      conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Provision text version`
`the provision text version read` MEANS
    IF reading AT MOST `the day the sources were last checked`
    THEN foldr `the later published of two provision text versions` NOTHING (filter (GIVEN v YIELD v's `published on` AT MOST reading AND v's `takes effect on` AT MOST conduct) versions)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN versions IS A LIST OF `Provision text version`
      conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`the source of the provision text version read` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` versions conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "NOTHING"
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `source`

