-- src:BA1994.20030731:1743 | Unauthorised decoders
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1744 | 48.—(1) No person shall, in the course of any trade or business,
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1745 | import, manufacture, sell, offer for sale or let for hire any
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1746 | unauthorised decoder.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1747 | (2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1748 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1749 | $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1750 | to both and any unauthorised decoder shall be forfeited to the
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1751 | Authority.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1752 | (3) Proof that a person has, in the course of any trade or business,
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1753 | imported, manufactured, sold, offered for sale or let for hire any
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1754 | unauthorised decoder shall be evidence that such person knew that
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1755 | the decoder was an unauthorised decoder.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1756 | (4) In this section —
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1757 | ‘‘decoder’’ means any apparatus or component part thereof
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1758 | which is designed or adapted to enable (whether on its own
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1764 | or with any other apparatus) an encrypted audio or visual
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1765 | programme to be decoded;
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1766 | ‘‘unauthorised decoder’’ means a decoder which will enable
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1767 | encrypted audio or visual programmes to be viewed in
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1768 | decoded form without payment of the subscription payable in
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1769 | respect of the right to view those programmes.
@ref s 48, Revised Edition 2003 (src:BA1994.20030731:1743-1769)
`s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003` MEANS
    `Provision text version` WITH `source` IS "s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003); there was no s 48A"
                                , `takes effect on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                , `published on` IS (Date 31 7 2003)
                                , `is the text after the amendment` IS FALSE

-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:44 | 2. Section 48 of the Broadcasting Act is repealed and the following
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:45 | sections substituted therefor:
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:47 | “Offences relating to unauthorised decoders and unauthorised
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:48 | reception of encrypted programmes
@ref Act 55 of 2004 s 2 (section 48 repealed and substituted, new section 48A) (src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:44-48)
`s 48 and s 48A as substituted by the Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004` MEANS
    `Provision text version` WITH `source` IS "s 48 and s 48A as substituted by Act 55 of 2004, in operation 1 January 2005 by S 750/2004"
                                , `takes effect on` IS `Act 55 of 2004 takes effect on`
                                , `published on` IS `S 750/2004 was first published on`
                                , `is the text after the amendment` IS TRUE

`the s 48 versions` MEANS LIST `s 48 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003`, `s 48 and s 48A as substituted by the Broadcasting (Amendment) Act 2004`

-- The prohibition in s 48(1) as the Revised Edition 2003 printed it: five acts, in the course of any trade or business, no element of knowledge.
-- The 2003 definition of "unauthorised decoder" (a decoder that will enable encrypted programmes to be viewed in decoded form without payment of the subscription) is the fact asked.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1744 | 48.—(1) No person shall, in the course of any trade or business,
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1745 | import, manufacture, sell, offer for sale or let for hire any
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1746 | unauthorised decoder.
@ref s 48(1), Revised Edition 2003 (src:BA1994.20030731:1744-1746)
GIVEN act IS A `Act with a decoder`
      `the act is done in the course of any trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` MEANS
    `the act is done in the course of any trade or business` AND `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder`
    AND (CONSIDER act
         WHEN `import` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `manufacture` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `sell` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `offer for sale` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `let for hire` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- src:BA1994.20030731:1752 | (3) Proof that a person has, in the course of any trade or business,
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1753 | imported, manufactured, sold, offered for sale or let for hire any
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1754 | unauthorised decoder shall be evidence that such person knew that
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1755 | the decoder was an unauthorised decoder.
@ref s 48(3), Revised Edition 2003 (proof is evidence of knowledge) (src:BA1994.20030731:1752-1755)
GIVEN act IS A `Act with a decoder`
      `it is proved that the person did the act in the course of any trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48(3) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, proof of the act is evidence that the person knew the decoder was an unauthorised decoder` MEANS
    `it is proved that the person did the act in the course of any trade or business`
    AND (CONSIDER act
         WHEN `import` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `manufacture` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `sell` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `offer for sale` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `let for hire` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- The prohibition on a conduct day, the law read as at a day: the Revised Edition 2003 rule before 1 January 2005, the single-text rule of sgba-p11-offences.l4 from then.
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:49 | 48.—(1) No person shall manufacture, assemble, modify, import,
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:50 | export, sell, offer for sale, let for hire or otherwise distribute any
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:51 | decoder which he knows is an unauthorised decoder.
@ref s 48(1) as substituted, Act 55 of 2004 (src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:49-51)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
      act IS A `Act with a decoder`
      `the act is done in the course of any trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN
        IF v's `is the text after the amendment`
        THEN JUST (`s 48(1) the person's act is prohibited` act `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder` `the person knows the decoder is an unauthorised decoder`)
        ELSE JUST (`s 48(1) as printed in the Revised Edition 2003, the person's act is prohibited` act `the act is done in the course of any trade or business` `the decoder is an unauthorised decoder`)

-- The punishment is the same in both texts: a fine not exceeding $40,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 3 years or both, and forfeiture of the unauthorised decoder to the Authority.
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1747 | (2) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1748 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1749 | $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1750 | to both and any unauthorised decoder shall be forfeited to the
-- src:BA1994.20030731:1751 | Authority.
@ref s 48(2), Revised Edition 2003 (guilt and punishment) (src:BA1994.20030731:1747-1751)
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:56 | (3) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) shall be
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:57 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:58 | exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:59 | 3 years or to both, and any unauthorised decoder shall be forfeited to
-- src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:60 | the Authority.
@ref s 48(3) as substituted, Act 55 of 2004 (src:BA1994-ACT55-2004:56-60)
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 48 the punishment on conviction, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (`s 48(3) the punishment on conviction`)

-- Section 48A did not exist before 1 January 2005: nothing in the Revised Edition 2003 gives the civil action.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A is part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision text version read` `the s 48 versions` conduct reading
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST v THEN JUST (v's `is the text after the amendment`)

